<%# THE CHANNEL AS THE CUSTOMER SEES IT.

  WHY THIS IS DRAWN AND EVERY OTHER PICTURE ON THE SITE IS PHOTOGRAPHED. The rest of the page shows the
  agent's screen, and those are real captures because that screen is ours to photograph. This is the other
  end of the conversation -- a customer's own phone -- and there is no honest screenshot of it to take. So it
  is drawn, and the section says in the reader's language exactly what it is drawing: the shape of an
  approved WhatsApp template, which this product builds, validates and sends.

  AND THE SHAPE IS NOT INVENTED. A template is HEADER / BODY / FOOTER / BUTTONS, buttons are QUICK_REPLY, URL,
  PHONE_NUMBER or COPY_CODE, and there may be up to ten of them -- Whatsapp::Templates::Validator:20-25. The
  preview shows an image header, a body with a variable filled in, a footer and two quick replies, because
  that is a template this product can actually produce.

  THE WORDS IN THE PHONE ARE IN THE LOCALE FILE, not in the operator's fields. It is an illustration of a
  message format; an operator editing a delivery time or a price into it would be writing an unreviewed claim
  into a picture. The operator owns the heading, the standfirst, the four points and the link.

  THE BRAND MARK IS NOMINATIVE. WhatsApp's own mark names the channel this is a message on, from the one
  place every channel mark on this site lives, so the preview cannot show a logo for a channel the
  installation does not support.
%>
<% mark = Marketing::ChannelBrand.marked?(:whatsapp) %>
<% link = marketing_target_href(section['link_target']) %>
<% points = Array(section['items']).filter_map { |item| item['title'].presence }.first(4) %>

<section class="<%= tone %>">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-20 sm:px-6 lg:py-24">
    <div class="grid items-center gap-14 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_22rem] lg:gap-20">
      <div>
        <% if section['kicker'].present? %>
          <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-lyn-royal"><%= section['kicker'] %></p>
        <% end %>
        <% if section['heading'].present? %>
          <h2 class="mt-3 text-balance text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-lyn-ink sm:text-4xl">
            <%= section['heading'] %>
          </h2>
        <% end %>
        <% if section['lede'].present? %>
          <p class="mt-5 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-lyn-ink-soft"><%= section['lede'] %></p>
        <% end %>

        <% if points.any? %>
          <ul class="mt-8 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
            <% points.each do |point| %>
              <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                <%# The tick is the only mark in this list and it is decoration: the sentence beside it is the
                    content, so it is hidden rather than labelled nine times over. %>
                <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24"
                     class="mt-0.5 size-5 flex-none text-lyn-indigo" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                     stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <path d="m20 6-11 11-5-5"/>
                </svg>
                <span class="text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-lyn-ink"><%= point %></span>
              </li>
            <% end %>
          </ul>
        <% end %>

        <% if link.present? && section['link_label'].present? %>
          <a href="<%= link %>"
             class="mt-8 inline-flex min-h-11 items-center gap-2 text-base font-semibold text-lyn-royal transition-colors hover:text-lyn-indigo-deep focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-lyn-blue">
            <%= section['link_label'] %>
            <svg aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-4 rtl:-scale-x-100"
                 fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
              <path d="M5 12h13m0 0-5-5m5 5-5 5"/>
            </svg>
          </a>
        <% end %>
      </div>

      <%# THE PHONE.

          `dir="ltr"` IS DELIBERATE AND NOT A BUG. A WhatsApp thread puts the other party's messages on the
          left and yours on the right in both writing directions -- the app does not mirror its thread -- so
          mirroring this preview under Arabic would be drawing a screen the reader has never seen. The Arabic
          TEXT inside it still reads right-to-left, because each bubble carries the paragraph direction of its
          own content.

          THE WHOLE DEVICE IS `aria-hidden`. It is an illustration of a message format; the points beside it
          carry the meaning, and reading a drawing of a phone aloud -- chrome, timestamps, tick marks -- tells
          a screen-reader user nothing they are not already being told in a sentence. %>
      <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[20rem]">
        <%# `aria-hidden` SITS ON THE DEVICE AND NOT ON THIS COLUMN, because the note below it is the one
            sentence a reader who cannot see the picture needs -- and `aria-hidden` on an ancestor cannot be
            undone by a descendant, so a note inside the device would have been hidden with it. %>
        <div class="rounded-[2.25rem] bg-lyn-ink p-2.5 shadow-[0_40px_80px_-30px_rgba(10,23,51,0.55)]"
             aria-hidden="true" dir="ltr">
          <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-[1.75rem] bg-[#ECE5DD]">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 bg-lyn-ink px-4 py-3 text-lyn-paper">
              <% if mark %>
                <%= render 'marketing/shared/channel_mark', id: :whatsapp, size: 28, labelled: false %>
              <% end %>
              <div class="min-w-0">
                <p class="truncate text-sm font-semibold"><%= "#{t('marketing.brand.name')} #{t('marketing.brand.suffix')}" %></p>
                <p class="truncate text-[0.7rem] text-lyn-paper/60"><%= t('marketing.device.whatsapp.account') %></p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="space-y-2 px-3 py-4">
              <div class="max-w-[90%] rounded-2xl rounded-ss-sm bg-white p-2.5 shadow-sm">
                <%# THE IMAGE HEADER, drawn as the placeholder it is rather than as a stock photograph: a
                    template's header is whatever media the sender attaches, and inventing a product shot here
                    would be inventing a customer's catalogue. %>
                <div class="flex h-20 items-center justify-center rounded-xl bg-gradient-to-br from-lyn-royal to-lyn-indigo text-[0.7rem] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-white/90">
                  <%= t('marketing.device.whatsapp.header') %>
                </div>
                <p class="mt-2.5 text-[0.82rem] leading-relaxed text-lyn-ink" dir="auto">
                  <%= t('marketing.device.whatsapp.body') %>
                </p>
                <p class="mt-2 text-[0.68rem] text-lyn-ink-soft/70" dir="auto">
                  <%= t('marketing.device.whatsapp.footer') %>
                </p>
                <p class="mt-1 text-end text-[0.62rem] text-lyn-ink-soft/60">10:30</p>
              </div>

              <%# THE QUICK REPLIES, drawn as the buttons WhatsApp renders under a template rather than as
                  controls: nothing here is operable, and a <button> in a picture is a tab stop that does
                  nothing when it is reached. %>
              <div class="max-w-[90%] space-y-1">
                <% t('marketing.device.whatsapp.buttons').each do |label| %>
                  <p class="rounded-xl bg-white py-2 text-center text-[0.78rem] font-medium text-[#1d8aed] shadow-sm" dir="auto">
                    <%= label %>
                  </p>
                <% end %>
              </div>

              <div class="ms-auto flex max-w-[85%] items-end gap-1.5 rounded-2xl rounded-ee-sm bg-[#D9FDD3] p-2.5 shadow-sm">
                <p class="text-[0.82rem] leading-relaxed text-lyn-ink" dir="auto">
                  <%= t('marketing.device.whatsapp.reply') %>
                </p>
                <span class="flex flex-none items-center gap-0.5 self-end pb-0.5 text-[0.62rem] text-lyn-ink-soft/60">
                  10:32
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 20 14" class="size-3.5 text-[#53bdeb]" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                       stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" focusable="false">
                    <path d="M1 7.6 4.4 11 11 3.4"/>
                    <path d="M8.4 7.9 10.6 11 19 1.6"/>
                  </svg>
                </span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <% if section['note'].present? %>
          <p class="mt-4 text-center text-[0.8rem] leading-relaxed text-lyn-ink-soft" dir="auto">
            <%= section['note'] %>
          </p>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
